This study examines the semileptonic decays of doubly charmed baryons, specifically $\Xi_{cc}^{++}$, $\Omega_{cc}^{+}$, and $\Xi_{cc}^{+}$, utilizing the Pouch model. We calculate the form factors for these processes and derive the corresponding decay widths. Our findings indicate that the decay width for $\Xi_{cc}^{++} 	o \Xi_{c}^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$ is approximately $1.0 	imes 10^{-14}$ GeV, while the width for $\Omega_{cc}^{+} 	o \Xi_{c}^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$ is roughly $1.0 	imes 10^{-14}$ GeV. Additionally, the decay width for $\Xi_{cc}^{+} 	o \Xi_{c}^{+} \ell^{+} 
u_{\ell}$ is estimated to be around $1.0 	imes 10^{-14}$ GeV. These results provide valuable insights into the dynamics of doubly charmed baryon decays and may assist in future experimental searches.
